id=\"edition-interpretive-simple-lemmatized\">  <div class=\"textpart\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <span data-text=\"Θεοῖς\" data-n=\"5\" data-lemma=\"θεός\">Θεοῖς</span>  <span data-text=\"καταχθονίοις\" data-n=\"10\" data-lemma=\"καταχθόνιος\">καταχθονίοις</span>  <span data-text=\"Δαίμοσι\" data-n=\"12\" data-lemma=\"δαιμόνιος\">Δαίμοσι</span>  <span data-text=\"Βειψάνιος\" data-n=\"15\" data-lemma=\"Βειψάνιος\">Βειψάνιος</span>  <span data-text=\"Ζώτικος\" data-n=\"20\" data-lemma=\"Ζώτικος\">Ζώτικος</span>  <span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\" data-n=\"25\" data-lemma=\"ζάω\">ἔζησεν</span>  <span data-text=\"ἔτη\" data-n=\"30\" data-lemma=\"ἔτος\">ἔτη</span>  <span data-text=\"λ\" data-n=\"40\" data-lemma=\"λ\">λ</span>  <span data-text=\"Ἡρακλεία\" data-n=\"50\" data-lemma=\"Ἡρακλεία\">Ἡρακλεία</span>  <span data-text=\"ἀνδρὶ\" data-n=\"55\" data-lemma=\"ἀνήρ\">ἀνδρὶ</span>  <span data-text=\"εὐσεβεστάτῳ\" data-n=\"60\" data-lemma=\"εὐσεβής\">εὐσεβεστάτῳ</span>  </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"Θεοῖς\" data-n=\"5\" data-lemma=\"θεός\">Θ</span><span data-text=\"καταχθονίοις\" data-n=\"10\" data-lemma=\"καταχθόνιος\">Κ.</span><span data-text=\"Δαίμοσι\" data-n=\"12\" data-lemma=\"δαιμόνιος\">Δ</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Βειψάνιος\n                    Ζώτικος\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Βειψάνιος\"><span data-text=\"Βειψάνιος\" data-n=\"15\" data-lemma=\"Βειψάνιος\">ΒΕΙΨΑΝΙΟ[.]</span></span><br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ζώτικος\"><span data-text=\"Ζώτικος\" data-n=\"20\" data-lemma=\"Ζώτικος\">ΖΩΤΙΚΟΣ</span></span></span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\" data-n=\"25\" data-lemma=\"ζάω\">[......]</span><br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\" data-n=\"30\" data-lemma=\"ἔτος\">ΕΤΗ</span>·<span data-text=\"λ\" data-n=\"40\" data-lemma=\"λ\">Λ</span>·<span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἡρακλεία\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἡρακλεία\"><span data-text=\"Ἡρακλεία\" data-n=\"50\" data-lemma=\"Ἡρακλεία\">ΗΡΑΚΛ[...]</span></span></span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"ἀνδρὶ\" data-n=\"55\" data-lemma=\"ἀνήρ\">ΑΝΔΡΙ</span><span data-text=\"εὐσεβεστάτῳ\" data-n=\"60\" data-lemma=\"εὐσεβής\">ΕΥΣΕΒ[......]</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Victoria Fendel, Robert Crellin</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic-simple-lemmatized\"><div class=\"textpart\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><span data-text=\"Θεοῖς\" data-n=\"5\" data-lemma=\"θεός\">ΘΕΟΙΣ</span><span data-text=\"καταχθονίοις\" data-n=\"10\" data-lemma=\"καταχθόνιος\">ΚΑΤΑΧΘΟΝΙΟΙΣ</span><span data-text=\"Δαίμοσι\" data-n=\"12\" data-lemma=\"δαιμόνιος\">ΔΑΙΜΟΣΙ</span><span data-text=\"Βειψάνιος\" data-n=\"15\" data-lemma=\"Βειψάνιος\">ΒΕΙΨΑΝΙΟΣ</span><span data-text=\"Ζώτικος\" data-n=\"20\" data-lemma=\"Ζώτικος\">ΖΩΤΙΚΟΣ</span><span data-text=\"ἔζησεν\" data-n=\"25\" data-lemma=\"ζάω\">ΕΖΗΣΕΝ</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\" data-n=\"30\" data-lemma=\"ἔτος\">ΕΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"λ\" data-n=\"40\" data-lemma=\"λ\">Λ</span><span data-text=\"Ἡρακλεία\" data-n=\"50\" data-lemma=\"Ἡρακλεία\">ΗΡΑΚΛΕΙΑ</span><span data-text=\"ἀνδρὶ\" data-n=\"55\" data-lemma=\"ἀνήρ\">ΑΝΔΡΙ</span><span data-text=\"εὐσεβεστάτῳ\" data-n=\"60\" data-lemma=\"εὐσεβής\">ΕΥΣΕΒΕΣΤΑΤΩ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span class=\"line 1\">line.1: <span>ΘΚΔ lapis; Θ(εοῖς) Κα̣(ταχθονίοις) CIG III 5709, IG XIV 495</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 5\">line.5: <span>ἀνδρὶ εὐσεβ[εστάτῳ IG XIV 495; ἀνδρὶ εὐσε[βεῖ Amico; ἀνδρὶ εὐσε[βεῖ μνήμης χάριν CIG III 5709</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2> translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>To the Underworld Gods. Vipsanius Zotikos lived for 30 years. Herakleia (set this up) for her most devoted husband.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The epitaph was dedicated by his wife, Herakleia, to her husband, Vispanius Zotikos, who was probably a freedman of the gens Vipsania, whose members were well represented at Catania. This is unsurprising, as Vipsanius Agrippa owned estates in the area (see Salmeri 1984, 18–19), and is further confirmed by other Imperial-period funerary inscriptions mentioning individuals of the Vipsanii (IG XIV 494; IMusCatania 146; CIL X 2, 7101). The epitaph belongs to Formula G4 in Korhonen’s classification (2004, 86–87). It comprises an invocation to the gods — in the otherwise unparalleled abbreviated form <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ΘΚΔ</span>, which represents a conflation of the formulae <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Θ(εοῖς) Κ(αταχθονίοις)</span> and <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Θ(εοῖς) Δ(αίμοσι)</span> (the instances in SEG 52.903 and 905 are antiquarian forgeries derived from this text) — followed by the name of the deceased and his age, the name of the dedicator, and the deceased’s name in the dative accompanied by an expression specifying the relationship between the two. The header is reported as complete and intact by Carrera and there is therefore no inherent reason to doubt it, although the abbreviation <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Κα(ταχθονίοις)</span> is attested in ISic001152 from Termini Imerese and Carrera might have misread delta for alpha. The restoration proposed by Kaibel for line 5 (ap. IG XIV 495), <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">εὐσεβ[εστάτῳ]</span>, is particularly convincing, since at Catania the superlative of <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">εὐσεβής</span> is attested exclusively in this type of funerary formula (cf. Korhonen 2004, 90).</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Carrera 1639 289 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002755\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002755</a>  </li><li> Franz 1853 5709 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250</a>  </li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">495</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1988 49 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li> Korhonen 2004 86-87, 90 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001897\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001897</a>  </li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  </div>",
